READING GUIDE
-------------
The raw two-stroke figure preserves continuous tangent orientation.
If the second stroke is the negative of the first, the line has
returned while its arrow has reversed.

The aligned-stroke figure identifies w and -w. It therefore shows
the shared geometry of the stroke rather than its alternating
orientation.

